# Group by Company Feature

This feature adds user controls to group jobs by company on the Kanban board, specifically for columns where a company has multiple roles.

## Proposed Changes

### Hooks
#### [MODIFY] [useJobFilters.ts](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/hooks/useJobFilters.ts)
- Update [FilterState](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/hooks/useJobFilters.ts#4-13) to include `groupByCompany: boolean`.
- Initialize it to `false` and handle it in the [clearFilters](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/hooks/useJobFilters.ts#78-89) method.

### Components
#### [MODIFY] [FilterBar.tsx](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/components/layout/FilterBar.tsx)
- Add a new toggle button labeled "Group by Company" next to the existing "Has Resume" filter button.
- Toggling this update the `groupByCompany` state via [setFilter](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/hooks/useJobFilters.ts#74-77).

#### [MODIFY] [Dashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/components/Dashboard.tsx)
- Pass the new `groupByCompany={filters.groupByCompany}` prop into the `<KanbanBoard />` component.

#### [MODIFY] [KanbanBoard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx)
- Add `groupByCompany?: boolean` to [KanbanBoardProps](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx#16-25).
- Add local state to track collapsed company groups: `const [collapsedGroups, setCollapsedGroups] = useState<Record<string, boolean>>({});`.
- Update the column rendering logic to evaluate `columnJobs`:
  - If `groupByCompany` is true, group `columnJobs` by `job.company`.
  - For each company in that column:
    - If the company has > 1 role in this column, render a collapsible header containing the company name and role count. Clicking this toggles the collapsed state for `[column.status]-[company]`. Render its jobs underneath (if expanded).
    - If the company has 1 role, just render the single job card without a collapsible header.
  - Re-attach the drag-and-drop handlers properly to the new grouped layout.

# City Auto-fill Feature

This feature fixes a bug in the city search where obscure cities were prioritized and integrates the updated autocomplete selector into the manual Add Job form.

## Proposed Changes

### Components
#### [MODIFY] [CityAutocomplete.tsx](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/components/CityAutocomplete.tsx)
- Modify the search algorithm to collect matches rather than returning the first 8 occurrences found alphabetically.
- Rank matches prioritizing: exact matches or `startsWith` over `includes`, then prioritize US country code, then ascending alphabetical order.
- Slice the top 8 matches after sorting them properly.

#### [MODIFY] [AddJobModal.tsx](file:///c:/Users/adira/Desktop/REPOSITORIES/blip/src/components/AddJobModal.tsx)
- Replace the standard `<input>` for the "Location" field with the `<CityAutocomplete>` component.
- Ensure the selected autocomplete location correctly ties back to `formData.location`.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Open the application and add multiple jobs for the same company (e.g., "Google") and give them the same status (e.g., "BACKLOG").
2. Ensure there's a column with >1 role for Google, and another company like "Meta" with only 1 role in the same column.
3. Click the "Group by Company" button in the FilterBar.
4. Verify that Google is now grouped under a collapsible header, and Meta is rendered normally.
5. Toggle the collapsible header to ensure child cards appear/disappear.
6. Verify dragging and dropping cards (including those in groups) still correctly changes their status and updates the UI.
7. Open the Add Job Modal via the manual entry button.
8. Type "san fran" in the Location field. Validate that San Francisco, CA, US is the primary suggestion, instead of a Brazilian city. Check that selecting a city correctly populates the value and persists on save.
